data.content:
Here's what breaks in EF Core 10 and how to fix each piece:

---

## 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — no longer accepts expression trees

**What broke:** The parameter changed from `Expression<Func<...>>` to a plain `Func<...>`. Your manual expression tree code won't compile.

**Fix — use a regular lambda with statements:**

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

No more `Expression.Lambda` / `Expression.Call` gymnastics needed.

---

## 2. Complex type columns — names are now uniquified & nested paths changed

**What broke:**
- Properties with the same name across complex types (e.g. `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street`) now get a disambiguating suffix instead of silently sharing a column.
- Nested complex types now use the **full path** in column names: `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` → column `Payment_BillingAddress_City` (was just `BillingAddress_City`).

This means new migrations will try to rename existing columns.

**Fix — pin the old column names explicitly:**

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, p =>
        p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, p =>
        p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
});

// For nested complex types, pin the old (short) name:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

**What broke:** All methods (`CommandReaderExecuting`, `CommandReaderExecuted`, etc.) now require an additional `string logCommandText` parameter (contains redacted SQL for logging).

**Fix:**

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)          // ← add this
    {
        // Use logCommandText for logging (sensitive data redacted)
        // Use command.CommandText for actual execution SQL
    }
}
```

Add the same parameter to every method on the interface (`CommandScalarExecuting`, `CommandNonQueryExecuting`, etc.).
